{"id": "EUVD-2026-81760", "enisaUuid": "15dc86f1-846b-3c56-9171-99307692771b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: serialize oplock close with pending break ownership\n\nclose may abort an in-flight oplock break while another breaker already\nholds an opinfo reference. Releasing pending_break wakes that waiter, but\nwithout serializing the close transition with bit acquisition it can become\na new break owner through the test_and_set_bit() fast path. It can then\noverwrite OPLOCK_CLOSING with OPLOCK_ACK_WAIT and continue a break for\na dying opinfo.\n\nMake OPLOCK_CLOSING terminal once the opinfo is removed from the inode\nlist. Serialize that transition, pending_break acquisition, and\nOPLOCK_ACK_WAIT setup with an opinfo state lock. A breaker which loses\nthe race releases its ownership and returns -ENOENT. Explicitly wake\npending_break waiters during close so they can observe the terminal state.\n\nAlso prevent ACK and timeout paths from replacing OPLOCK_CLOSING with\nOPLOCK_STATE_NONE.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:16", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7148a6c06ddf1c263a1cf422bee541f24d3d3926", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7d6e682b7633120c2f93400b8c6f335d9d8e5318", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc1e34f78dfab755fab9ad820ac5f82348fe1792", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5f97bac88bfb333f426f01c118b8235e75af8d96", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b0148dc5625dbfd50596ac63c7487c12e8a8ab03"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90167", "GHSA-923f-jcq6-gqvq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08bc339f-769c-33df-b56d-5e87c5702605", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "10f55379-beab-3d01-9f42-87e328298dab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "27bca74a-acfd-3819-9f8b-8606b3e1b923", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "2d070582-2715-374d-a509-bb22b8ed01a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "6c2aaba8-d251-3d08-8aca-10a8138587c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "7760beb7-2b50-31e7-9082-d5fea90d8e89", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <7148a6c06ddf1c263a1cf422bee541f24d3d3926"}, {"id": "7f2b9e5e-cc1b-3ee4-86dd-64911d3004c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "8fde8d2c-d213-3d8a-babd-d2493abe112a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <5f97bac88bfb333f426f01c118b8235e75af8d96"}, {"id": "9d98e3e6-2ad2-37ea-ab00-3cb4435a70d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <7d6e682b7633120c2f93400b8c6f335d9d8e5318"}, {"id": "cbd8f7c8-827c-32f9-b8f2-922720c63557", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "de06b990-feb1-3918-87c2-82d32ebfc091", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <b0148dc5625dbfd50596ac63c7487c12e8a8ab03"}, {"id": "f40af19a-8a21-342f-b287-82d8a4c8a70f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <dc1e34f78dfab755fab9ad820ac5f82348fe1792"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1dc309b8-11a0-316b-b2ed-c2997284ed25", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}